{
  "_note": "Papyrus 66 (P66 / Bodmer II), page 1 (folio 1 recto, numbered 'alpha' by the ancient pagination), containing the opening of the Gospel of John. This file supports a 'Read P66 yourself' view synchronizing (1) a scriptio-continua transcription as the papyrus itself would show it, uppercase, unaccented, with nomina sacra, (2) the modern critical SBLGNT text from data/source-text.json, and (3) an English gloss, for John 1:1-5. The 'words' array links tokens 0-60 of source-text.json (John 1:1-5) to their p66 form/line/box. Lines beyond verse 5 (to fill out roughly the first 14 lines of the page) are given as running text only, with no word-level linkage, since source-text.json stops at verse 5.",
  "sources": [
    "Wikipedia, 'Papyrus 66' (manuscript description, date range, holding institution): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papyrus_66",
    "Wikimedia Commons, Category:Papyrus 66 (candidate facsimile images): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Papyrus_66",
    "SBL Greek New Testament, https://sblgnt.com (CC BY 4.0) -- modern comparison text, already in data/source-text.json",
    "General scholarly consensus on P66 palaeography (scriptio continua, nomina sacra ΘΣ/ΘΝ/ΘΥ with supralinear stroke, absence of accents/breathings in the first hand) as described in standard NT textual-criticism references (e.g. Comfort & Barrett, 'The Text of the Earliest New Testament Greek Manuscripts'); no internet access was available in this run to confirm an exact published line-by-line transcription of page 1, see line_breaks_source and the image note below."
  ],
  "manuscript": {
    "ga": "P66",
    "name": "Papyrus Bodmer II",
    "date": "c. 200 AD (commonly cited range 150-250; some, e.g. Brent Nongbri, argue for a later date)",
    "holding": "Fondation Martin Bodmer, Cologny (Bibliotheca Bodmeriana), Switzerland",
    "page": "page 1 (recto, ancient pagination 'alpha'), containing the opening of John 1"
  },
