    "note": "Downloaded by .github/workflows/fetch-sources.yml (see data/fetched/p66-image.json). The photograph shows the whole codex at an angle, so the word boxes are drawn on the facsimile rendering, not on the photograph."
  },
  "line_breaks_source": "approximate -- no live network access was available in this run to consult a published line-by-line transcription of P66 page 1 (e.g. IGNTP/ITSEE at iohannes.com, the NTVMR at ntvmr.uni-muenster.de, or Comfort & Barrett's edition), since those hosts were also blocked by the egress policy. The Greek wording per verse is the standard John 1:1-9 text (no invented variant readings), rendered uppercase, without accents/breathings, with nomina sacra (ΘΝ/ΘΣ/ΘΥ) as P66's first hand is known to use; but the actual character-count-per-line and the exact points where words break across lines are a plausible reconstruction (~20-26 letters/line, 14 lines), not a transcription of the real photograph.",
